From f5d99934d2c191e75e601fcc38677da4f6b2752d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marc Britten <11667518+marcbritten@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 11:30:46 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix(project): save a project through a temp file and a
 rename

project::save wrote the project with std::fs::write. That call truncates
the old file first. A write that stopped (a full disk, a lost network
share, a stopped app) left a damaged project and no old copy.

project::save now writes through machine::store::write_atomic: a temp
file in the same folder, flushed, then renamed over the target. Machine
files, preferences, recent files and view settings already use it. The
window, the MCP tool save_project and the script call cam.save all go
through project::save.

Two refusals of the plain write stay. A folder that does not exist is
refused by name, because write_atomic creates missing folders. A
read-only project file is refused by name, because on Linux and macOS a
rename replaces a read-only file.

machine::store::temp_path_for gives the temp path. write_atomic uses it,
and the tests use it to make a save fail. A path that names no file is
now refused by name before a folder is made.

Fixes #3509

