From eab5f1932ca003145b6a6d42e14e3b44e4696a63 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 19:08:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix(project): probe write access before the atomic save

`project::save` now opens an existing project file for writing, with no
truncate and no create, before it writes the temp file. A file that this
process cannot write is refused as read-only, so the rename never replaces
it. This pins the shared-folder case: alice owns `/shared/job.camproj`
with mode 0644, bob saves from CamCraft, and alice's project stays.
`Permissions::readonly()` alone misses that file on Unix, because its mode
has a write bit and the rename needs write permission on the folder only.

The missing-folder refusal and the temp-file and rename stay unchanged.

Tests: `a_project_save_over_a_unix_socket_is_refused_and_kept` (red
before the probe: the rename replaced the socket) and
`a_project_save_into_a_folder_without_write_access_is_refused_and_kept`.
The cross-user case needs another uid and is not pinned.

Refs #3509

